    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294-a5">

                <pb facs="0490" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg418"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lincoln to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1882-04-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 18, 1882</date>. (Received April
                        21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of the 1st ultimo,
                    inclosing a copy of a note from the-Mexican minister reporting depredations in
                    Mexico by Indians who escaped from the San Carlos Reservation, I have the honor
                    to inclose herewith, in connection with reports on the subject heretofore
                    transmitted to you, copy of a letter from the General of the Army, dated Tucson,
                    Ariz., April 11, 1882, to whom a copy of your letter and its inclosure was
                    furnished.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBERT T. LINCOLN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        War</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
